arameterSuppliersFromTypedDataWithDefaultChecks` introduces new parameters (`nullsExpectedType`, `evaluatorToString`) that are not used within the method body. This could lead to confusion and unnecessary complexity if these parameters are intended for future use but are currently unused.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractScalarFunctionTestCase.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractScalarFunctionTestCase.java--3181:4228","promptId":"#7H6AN","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractScalarFunctionTestCase.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractScalarFunctionTestCase.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":3181,"endPos":4228,"startLine":77,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":99,"endLineOffset":5,"length":1048}]}]},{"comment":"The class `Percentile` is defined twice in the same file with the same content. This is redundant and should be removed to avoid duplication.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Percentile.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Percentile.java--2038:2057","promptId":"#9YFFP","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Percentile.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Percentile.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2038,"endPos":2057,"startLine":37,"startLineOffset":60,"endLine":37,"endLineOffset":79,"length":20}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Percentile.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Percentile.java--2027:2037","promptId":"#NFSGA","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Percentile.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/aggregate/Percentile.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2027,"endPos":2037,"startLine":37,"startLineOffset":49,"endLine":37,"endLineOffset":59,"length":11}]}]},{"comment":"The transformation of the expression using `FoldNull` is moved to before type resolution, which could potentially lead to different behavior if `FoldNull` affects the type resolution process. Ensure that moving this transformation does not inadvertently change how type resolution works.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractAggregationTestCase.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractAggregationTestCase.java-13529:13574,13583:13651-13322:13410,13419:13484,13493:13561","promptId":"#PXWBE","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractAggregationTestCase.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/AbstractAggregationTestCase.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":13529,"endPos":13574,"startLine":309,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":309,"endLineOffset":53,"length":46},{"pos":13583,"endPos":13651,"startLine":310,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":310,"endLineOffset":76,"length":69}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":13322,"endPos":13410,"startLine":304,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":304,"endLineOffset":96,"length":89},{"pos":13419,"endPos":13484,"startLine":305,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":305,"endLineOffset":73,"length":66},{"pos":13493,"endPos":13561,"startLine":306,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":306,"endLineOffset":76,"length":69}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":95,"line":104,"comment_lines":["[][104]"],"review_comment":["Percentile seems to require a foldable `percentile` value. Just curious why mv_percentile can accept even fields.","In the agg case, it\u0027s because it\u0027s \"impossible\" for it to not be foldable (Unless it appears in the grouping, which is a case I\u0027m not sure we\u0027re allowing btw).\r\nThe evaluator however, can handle them without problem, so I think it\u0027s better to just allow it. Simpler function, less arbitrary restrictions","I\u0027m not saying it\u0027s wrong, but maybe suggest to look at this from a different angle: language consistency. If one function does it one way and the other does it differently, we should try to be consistent and have the same behavior; this makes it less confusing for users and easier to use/adopt.","The consistent way for me would be to not force foldables on non-agg functions, as they all can be evaluated whether foldable or not. If I as a user tried to use a field in a function, and it told me that it must be a constant, _that_ would be confusing 👀 \r\nFor aggs, it\u0027s a logical problem, as they need X fields to accumulate, and Y fields as configuration.\r\n\r\nSo I\u0027m really not seeing the problem of having non-foldable fields. I feel like we would be placing arbitrary restrictions","Since `PERCENTILE` has to hit the whole index it has to be foldable. `MV_PERCENTILE` doesn\u0027t really have to be. But it\u0027s certainly kindest if, when it is, we can fail the query up front for invalid stuff.\r\n\r\nI\u0027m kind of ambivalent on forcing it to be foldable - I like that if we force it now we can always un-force it later. We can\u0027t go the other way. But in a lot of ways that\u0027s actually more work for a less flexible system."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/scalar/multivalue/MvPercentile.java","id":37448,"created_at":"2024-08-12T15:24:55Z","original_position":95,"side":"RIGHT","position":104,"submitted_on_commit":"b96fee395bf9474022d9e8c5e1ed20c9c359df52","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,391 @@\n+/*\n+ * Copyright Elasticsearch B.V. and/or licensed to Elasticsearch B.V. under one\n+ * or more contributor license agreements. Licensed under the Elastic License\n+ * 2.0; you may not use this file except in compliance with the Elastic License\n+ * 2.0.\n+ */\n+\n+package org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.scalar.multivalue;\n+\n+import org.elasticsearch.common.io.stream.NamedWriteableRegistry;\n+import org.elasticsearch.common.io.stream.StreamInput;\n+import org.elasticsearch.common.io.stream.StreamOutput;\n+import org.elasticsearch.compute.ann.Evaluator;\n+import org.elasticsearch.compute.data.DoubleBlock;\n+import org.elasticsearch.compute.data.IntBlock;\n+import org.elasticsearch.compute.data.LongBlock;\n+import org.elasticsearch.compute.operator.EvalOperator.ExpressionEvaluator;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.EsqlIllegalArgumentException;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.expression.Expression;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.tree.NodeInfo;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.tree.Source;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.type.DataType;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.Example;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.FunctionInfo;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.Param;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.expression.function.scalar.EsqlScalarFunction;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.io.stream.PlanStreamInput;\n+import org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.planner.PlannerUtils;\n+\n+import java.io.IOException;\n+import java.math.BigDecimal;\n+import java.util.Arrays;\n+import java.util.List;\n+import java.util.function.Function;\n+\n+import static org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.expression.TypeResolutions.ParamOrdinal.FIRST;\n+import static org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.expression.TypeResolutions.ParamOrdinal.SECOND;\n+import static org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.expression.TypeResolutions.isType;\n+import static org.elasticsearch.xpack.esql.core.type.DataType.UNSIGNED_LONG;\n+\n+public class MvPercentile extends EsqlScalarFunction {\n+    public static final NamedWriteableRegistry.Entry ENTRY \u003d new NamedWriteableRegistry.Entry(\n+        Expression.class,\n+        \"MvPercentile\",\n+        MvPercentile::new\n+    );\n+\n+    /**\n+     * 2^52 is the smallest integer where it and all smaller integers can be represented exactly as double\n+     */\n+    private static final double MAX_SAFE_LONG_DOUBLE \u003d Double.longBitsToDouble(0x4330000000000000L);\n+\n+    private final Expression field;\n+    private final Expression percentile;\n+\n+    @FunctionInfo(\n+        returnType \u003d { \"double\", \"integer\", \"long\" },\n+        description \u003d \"Converts a multivalued field into a single valued field containing \"\n+            + \"the value at which a certain percentage of observed values occur.\",\n+        examples \u003d @Example(file \u003d \"mv_percentile\", tag \u003d \"example\")\n+    )\n+    public MvPercentile(\n+        Source source,\n+        @Param(name \u003d \"number\", type \u003d { \"double\", \"integer\", \"long\" }, description \u003d \"Multivalue expression.\") Expression field,\n+        @Param(name \u003d \"percentile\", type \u003d { \"double\", \"integer\", \"long\" }) Expression percentile\n+    ) {\n+        super(source, List.of(field, percentile));\n+        this.field \u003d field;\n+        this.percentile \u003d percentile;\n+    }\n+\n+    private MvPercentile(StreamInput in) throws IOException {\n+        this(Source.readFrom((PlanStreamInput) in), in.readNamedWriteable(Expression.class), in.readNamedWriteable(Expression.class));\n+    }\n+\n+    @Override\n+    public String getWriteableName() {\n+        return ENTRY.name;\n+    }\n+\n+    @Override\n+    public void writeTo(StreamOutput out) throws IOException {\n+        source().writeTo(out);\n+        out.writeNamedWriteable(field);\n+        out.writeNamedWriteable(percentile);\n+    }\n+\n+    @Override\n+    protected Expression.TypeResolution resolveType() {\n+        if (childrenResolved() \u003d\u003d false) {\n+            return new TypeResolution(\"Unresolved children\");\n+        }\n+\n+        return isType(field, dt -\u003e dt.isNumeric() \u0026\u0026 dt !\u003d UNSIGNED_LONG, sourceText(), FIRST, \"numeric except unsigned_long\").and(\n+            isType(percentile, dt -\u003e dt.isNumeric() \u0026\u0026 dt !\u003d UNSIGNED_LONG, sourceText(), SECOND, \"numeric except unsigned_long\")","submitted_line":95},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"In the `processDoubles`, `processInts`, and `processLongs` methods, there is a repeated pattern of checking if `percentile \u003d\u003d 0` or `percentile \u003d\u003d 100`. This can be refactored into a separate method to reduce code duplication.","nodes":[{"id":"-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/scalar/multivalue/MvPercentile.java--1973:16406","promptId":"#NJN3B","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/function/scalar/multivalue/MvPercentile.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1973,"endPos":16406,"startLine":41,"startLineOffset":0,"endLine":391,"endLineOffset":1,"length":14434}]}]}]},{"groundTruth":{"original_line":37,"line":37,"comment_lines":["[][37]"],"review_comment":["I wonder if those are too much... As it\u0027s adding 4 times the amount of cases","Interesting! I can see why you\u0027d do it. What\u0027s the runtime difference on one of the tests? I can imagine it\u0027s a few seconds so it\u0027s worth it.\r\n\r\nAnother option is to randomize this bit. That\u0027s less cases at least.","On second inspection `AbstractMultivalueTestCase`\u0027s generators already have this. So I\u0027d just keep it and not worry about it. For MV functions it\u0027s quite an important bit of their behavior."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/jav